 RunRefresh dummy;ISODateTime;again;state
⍝ Serialised refresh worker. Spawned with & by Refresh.
⍝ Holds the refresh serialisation lock. If the pending flag
⍝ is set by the end of a refresh, this function loops and refreshes again.
⍝ dummy: ignored
 ISODateTime←##.ISODateTime
 state←##.GLOBAL.refresh
 :Repeat
     state.pending←0                  ⍝ This cycle satisfies any trigger queued so far
     state.started_at←⊃ISODateTime ⎕TS
     state.finished_at←⊂'null'
    ⍝ Blanket trap: this thread has no request and no OnErrorFn, so an escaping error
    ⍝ would hold the lock forever.
     :Trap 0
         RefreshData ##.GLOBAL.build_in_isolate
         state.last_success_at←⊃ISODateTime ⎕TS
         state.last_error_message←''
     :Else
         state.last_error_at←⊃ISODateTime ⎕TS
         state.last_error_message←⎕DMX.(EM,': ',Message)
         ##.Log'[REFRESH] ',state.last_error_message
     :EndTrap
     state.finished_at←⊃ISODateTime ⎕TS
     :Hold '#.DCMS.GLOBAL.refresh'
         :If again←state.pending
             state.pending←0
         :Else
             state.(running thread)←0 ¯1
         :EndIf
     :EndHold
 :Until ~again
